 microsatellite alleles in <italic>Drosophila melanogaster </italic>have a downward mutation bias and short persistence times, which cause their genome-wide underrepresentation</article-title><source>Genetics</source><year>2000</year><volume>155</volume><fpage>1213</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10880482</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jurka</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pethiyagoda</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Simple repetitive DNA sequences from primates: compilation and analysis</article-title><source>J Mol Evol</source><year>1995</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>120</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7699718</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF00167107</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pupko</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Graur</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evolution of microsatellites in the yeast <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic>: role of length and number of repeated units</article-title><source>J Mol Evol</source><year>1999</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>313</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10093220</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/PL00006474</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Katti</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ranjekar</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Gupta</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Differential distribution of simple sequence repeats in eukaryotic genome sequences</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><year>2001</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>1161